From: Rob Lymm <rob@mediaeden.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: wire the imx132 driver into the build

imx132.c was carried in this directory and copied into a kernel tree by
hand, with no Kconfig entry and no Makefile line. Nothing could build it
from a clean tree: dropping the source in and setting CONFIG_VIDEO_IMX132
in .config does nothing, because olddefconfig discards a symbol Kconfig
has never heard of, and the Makefile has no rule to reach the object.

That cost a build on 2026-09-20: thirteen of the fourteen media modules
rebuilt against a new kernel and the sensor silently did not, with no error
to say why.

Add the two lines it should always have had, modelled on VIDEO_IMX219,
which is the nearest sensor in the same family.

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig
@@ -148,6 +148,16 @@
 	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the
 	  module will be called imx214.
 
+config VIDEO_IMX132
+	tristate "Sony IMX132 sensor support"
+	select V4L2_CCI_I2C
+	help
+	  This is a Video4Linux2 sensor driver for the Sony
+	  IMX132 camera, the front sensor of the Xperia Z2.
+
+	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the
+	  module will be called imx132.
+
 config VIDEO_IMX219
 	tristate "Sony IMX219 sensor support"
 	select V4L2_CCI_I2C
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/Makefile
@@ -160,3 +160,4 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_VIDEO_VP27SMPX) += vp27smpx.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_VIDEO_VPX3220) += vpx3220.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_VIDEO_ZORAN) += zoran.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_VIDEO_IMX132) += imx132.o
